# Elastic Stack - (ELK)

- ELK was developed to store, search, and visualize large amounts of data.
- Organizations use it to monitor application performance and perform searches on large datasets.
> SOC analyst use ELK to perform log analysis and investigations.

# CORE ELEMENTS

E - Elasticsearch: full-text search and analytics engine for JSON-formatted documents.

L - Logstash: data processing engine that takes data from multiple sources, filters/normalizes it,
and then sends it to the destination (Kibana or listening port).

Beats - host-based agents (data-shippers) that ship/transfer data from endpoints to ELasticsearch.

K - Kibana: web-based data visualization toolthat works with Elasticsearch to analyze, investigate,
and visualize data streams in real time.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Discover Tab
- Shows ingested logs, search bar, and normalized fields.

> KQL - Kibana Query Language - search query language used to search ingested logs/documents in Elasticsearch.

- Free text search (text only - looks for the whole string)

    * - wildcard to match parts of the word
    Logcial Operators (AND | OR | NOT)

(i.e.) "United States" AND NOT ("Florida")

- Field-based search (Field: Value)
(i.e.) Source_ip: 238.163.231.224 AND UserName: Suleman

- Source_Country : United States AND UserName : James OR Albert
